// Ciccio's on-device portal (open AP "IndietroTutta", or the LAN when joined).
// The device is on DHCP and roams between the APs around the house, so this
// address changes without warning. Don't guess it and don't try to reach the
// old one: if it moved to another subnet, its portal is unreachable and you
// have nothing to query. Ask the DEV BACKEND instead — it records the LAN IP
// of every heartbeat, and the device is already talking to it in devl mode:
//
//   curl http://localhost:3000/devices | jq -r '.[]|"\(.ip) \(.status)"'
//
// then put the `ip` value below. `ssid`/`password` are only used by the
// Wi-Fi setup routes; the device joins a saved network on boot.
vars {
  baseUrl: http://192.168.0.106
  ssid: MyNetwork
  password: change-me
  username: Test Boat
  timezoneOffset: 1
}
